prompt='''Evaluate generated-video measurement usability and the closed laptop initially on the tabletop to the right of the green book. Images are synchronized PAIRS: even index is the full frame, next odd index is a fixed enlarged table-edge crop at the SAME time. Crop red outlines are SAM2 predictions from an initial box; masks may drift on corrupted videos and a box is NOT proof of identity, contact or motion. Use full frames to inspect scene continuity and cropped pixels for target pose. No previous model result or reference outcome is supplied.
First assess integrity. Definite fusion into background, disintegration, discontinuous target replacement, or severe scene geometry/texture collapse preventing event measurement is definite_corruption. Do not explain visible corruption away as camera movement. Ordinary camera motion, occlusion, rotation, color change or leaving the fixed crop alone is not corruption. If full frames do not resolve ambiguity use uncertain. Bad appearance alone is not enough. If corruption is definite, use unobservable support and cite at least two DISTINCT native frames demonstrating corruption; no fall label is needed.
If the target is intact and trackable, inspect actual pixels for support and motion. A thin dark underside may still be the target. Downward rotation or a box crossing the tabletop does not by itself prove complete loss of support. Distinguish clearly supported throughout, clear complete detachment with descent, ambiguous edge contact, and unobservable. Landing is not required when detachment and descent are clear. Do not treat this question as a request for a fall to occur.
Return JSON only with observations; NEVER output fall, score or event_gate:
{"integrity":"intact / definite_corruption / uncertain", "corruption_evidence_indices":[], "target_at_end":"visible / partially_visible / not_visible / uncertain", "support_state":"supported / detached_descending / edge_contact_uncertain / unobservable", "evidence_image_indices":[0,24], "detachment_evidence_indices":[], "descent_evidence_indices":[], "reason":"specific observed continuity, contact, motion or corruption evidence"}.
Choose one enum value. For detached_descending cite at least one image with visible complete detachment and two DISTINCT times showing descent. Leave detachment indices empty if separation cannot be resolved. Cite image indices 0..25 from this list, not native frame IDs or timestamps. Program derives routing and scores. Unknown is permitted.'''
